  "interpretation_boundary": "Measurements compare independent, host-PDC-compensated Ableton exports of one installed Waves F6 Stereo VST3 instance over a deterministic 72-second composite arrangement. They establish one flat-default null boundary, one static Bell transfer, one internal-sidechain downward dynamic setting, time-local level changes, and host-reported latency at 48 kHz. The shared bypass was rendered from the same arrangement and chain before F6 loading; triangular dither prevents a bit-perfect null and therefore small residual noise is expected. The experiment does not establish external-sidechain routing, M/S or channel-link behavior, alternate band shapes, upward expansion, RTA behavior, automation, CPU cost, other formats/sample rates, or musical preference on real vocals."
